//   s04  a harp lullaby for the sleeping keeper; the pad and clock cut on 'Pull'; the lullaby sours as the candle
//        burns through the band (A-flat for A); two clashing drones (D against E-flat) on 'Two rooms', out after
//        'Pin back'; a soft wooden knock after 'shutters', then silence; the maxim over a single low D.
//   s05  two pizzicato clocks out of phase drift together; one drops out on 'zero' (the snapped thread); celld's
//        terrace in G (harp and pad, the same clock motif on D–G): a greener colour of the same idea.
//   s06  D minor; one clockwork step per printed stamp; T small when A's crown is lit; S (A-sus4) held while B's crown
//        stays dark, the piano A withheld above it; SILENCE on 'died'; a resolving cello line A → D on 'recovers';
